  "id": "group-norm",
  "term": "group norm",
  "definition": "A group norm is a shared attitude or pattern of behavior that a group pressures its members to follow. In a group where a person feels comfortable, this pressure can outweigh personal habits, moral restraints, or individual preferences.",
